      "id": "GENUS_SPHENODON",
      "name": "Sphenodon",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "The tuatara. Sole surviving member of order Rhynchocephalia, whose lineage diverged from lizards 240 million years ago. It lived alongside dinosaurs and outlasted them. Despite superficial similarity to lizards, it is a deeply distinct lineage with a unique tooth-row shearing mechanism, a fully photoreceptive third eye on the top of the head, and the slowest-evolving DNA of any known vertebrate. It grows until age 35 and commonly lives over 100 years.",
